@0    = ~Okay, <CHARNAME>? Can I have a word -- away from the others?~
@1    = ~So, I'm interested in you. You probably got that. Problem is, Fade. I don't trust her -- she's with the Shadow Thieves, she could be up to anything, you never know. If you're into hanging out with her ... well, I'm going to have to not hang out with you as much, because I don't want her tattling to her masters.~
@2    = ~I'm not sure where I stand with Fade, but I know I am interested in you, Faren.~
@3    = ~You're paranoid. I'm not about to jeopardise my relationship with her.~
@4    = ~That's good to know. Thanks, <CHARNAME> -- it'll make me sleep a little easier.~
@5    = ~Oh. Well, fair enough, I guess. You know what you want, and all that.~
@6    = ~So. You lived in Athkatla a long time?~
@7    = ~If that's a chat-up line, it's abysmally bad.~
@8    = ~Here, I'll show you a trick. Knife spins up, like so, twist round, and--~
@9    = ~--catch it on the tail, twirl it around, and presto!~
@10   = ~Hey, nice question-deflecting! And the trick was pretty neat, too.~
@11   = ~Oh, you know me -- I do my best.~
@12   = ~So, <CHARNAME>, I was thinking we could--~
@13   = ~Actually, don't worry about it.~
@14   = ~Hmmm? Oh, don't stop on my account.~
@15   = ~No -- that's okay. I don't want it getting back to Master Linvail. I'll talk when we've got some more privacy.~
@16   = ~Watch it, buster. You might have everyone else fooled with your "aw-shucks, I'm just a small-town guy with stars in my eyes" thing.~
@17   = ~Hey, you said it, not me.~
@18   = ~You might think you're better than the Shadow Thieves, but I bet you've broken your share of noses in your time. And worse.~
@19   = ~But I don't work for a guy with gold-plated swimming-pools, now do I?~
@20   = ~Oh, come on, I've seen those swimming-pools. They're silver-plated at best.~
